{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["The choicest first fruits of your land — from the seven species mentioned in the portion כי תבא: ולקחת מראשית כל פרי האדמה. When you go up on pilgrimage feet, then you bring your first fruits." "You shall not cook a kid in its mother's milk — the way of goats is to give birth to two kids together. They were accustomed to slaughter one of them, and since there is an abundance of milk in goats, as written: ודי חלב עזים ללחמך וגו׳, they were accustomed to cook it in its mother's milk — and the verse speaks according to what occurs in practice. The thing is disgraceful and gluttonous and voracious, to eat the mother's milk together with her young. And similar to this is: באותו ואת בנו, and sending away the nest. To teach you proper conduct the verse commanded; and since on pilgrimage they would eat many animals, Scripture warned in the portion of pilgrimage festivals not to cook and not to eat a kid in its mother's milk. And the same law applies to all meat in milk, as our Rabbis explained in Hullin."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:50.882358589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}